  message: "THE FILED FACT IS STALE AT dev eb520bc07c, and the staleness changes what is\nstill being asked. Recorded rather than acted on: this item is\nneeds_human_review and the remaining question is the owner's.\n\nTHIS ITEM SAYS (2026-08-04): \"Python's built-in taint catalogue declares 83\nsources. ZERO of them mention subprocess... So hypergumbo currently models data\nflows INTO a subprocess and does not model data flows OUT OF a subprocess.\"\n\nAT TIP THAT IS NO LONGER TRUE. python.yaml rows check_output, getoutput and\ngetstatusoutput under the ipc_recv section with simultaneous: true, and the row\nnote says so in as many words: \"returns the CHILD'S output, so the call is a\ntransfer as well as a launch and mints an untrusted_input source.\" The mint is\nmechanical - taint.py maps ipc_recv to untrusted_input. Filed under INV-lozat\nand ADR-0049 ruling 1, i.e. AFTER this item was written.\n\nSO THE HALF THIS ITEM ARGUED FOR IS PARTLY SHIPPED. Subprocess output IS a\ncatalogued untrusted_input source in Python, for the calls whose name alone\nsettles that they return the child's bytes.\n\nWHAT REMAINS OPEN, and it is the harder half this item already named:\n  1. THE ARGUMENT-SHAPE PROBLEM. run is deliberately excluded, and the\n     catalogue says why: its CompletedProcess.stdout is the child's bytes only\n     when the caller passed capture_output= or stdout=PIPE, \"and the catalogue\n     matches on name, not on keyword arguments. Rowing it would mint a source\n     at every subprocess.run call in the corpus, most of which capture\n     nothing.\" Popen.communicate is the same shape one hop worse - the\n     deciding argument is on the CONSTRUCTOR, not on the call.\n  2. THE SATURATION QUESTION, which is this item's own ARGUMENT AGAINST and is\n     untouched by the above.\n\nWHY IT CAME UP: WI-jabus needs subprocess.Popen declared before hypergumbo's\nown 18 self-claims can leave inconclusive, and I wanted to know whether rowing\ncommunicate would pre-empt this decision. It does not - the precedented\ntreatment is a launch-only row with the omission disclosed, exactly as run\nalready has. Noting it here so the next reader does not re-derive it.\n\nNO STATUS CHANGE. The threat-model question is still the owner's; only its\npremise needed correcting."  # d972
